1
00:00:00,773 --> 00:00:02,913
An accident? What accident?

2
00:00:03,113 --> 00:00:04,283
A car accident.

3
00:00:04,913 --> 00:00:08,923
His father died at the scene. He was the only survivor.

4
00:00:08,983 --> 00:00:10,783
What? A car accident?

5
00:00:10,883 --> 00:00:14,853
Yes. The trauma made him lose all his memories of the accident,

6
00:00:15,193 --> 00:00:18,323
but lately, it seems bits and pieces are coming back in his dreams.

7
00:00:19,593 --> 00:00:23,803
He even went to the police station to ask about the accident,

8
00:00:24,333 --> 00:00:26,873
but they just said the records from 25 years ago had been discarded.

9
00:00:26,933 --> 00:00:27,933
Wait a second.

10
00:00:29,043 --> 00:00:30,773
Twenty-five years ago would be...

11
00:00:32,243 --> 00:00:33,373
In 2001?

12
00:00:33,973 --> 00:00:37,443
Yes, when he was seven. What is it?

13
00:00:42,223 --> 00:00:45,253
- It's nothing. Go get some sleep. - But...

14
00:00:46,093 --> 00:00:48,653
Didn't you come here to tell me something?

15
00:00:48,863 --> 00:00:51,393
You must have had a hard day...

16
00:00:51,823 --> 00:00:53,463
with Team Leader Ko's parents objecting.

17
00:00:53,593 --> 00:00:56,203
No, I was prepared for that.

18
00:00:56,203 --> 00:00:58,463
But you saw us, right? We're unshakable.

19
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:01,073
- There's no reason for us to waver. - Good.

20
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:02,973
Still, it seems your feelings for each other...

21
00:01:02,973 --> 00:01:04,503
are deeper than I thought.

22
00:01:04,843 --> 00:01:06,713
Just as you've always believed in me,

23
00:01:06,713 --> 00:01:09,413
please believe in us now and watch over us.

24
00:01:09,943 --> 00:01:11,643
Okay, go get some sleep now.

25
00:01:11,983 --> 00:01:14,053
- Okay, good night. - All right.

26
00:01:26,263 --> 00:01:28,063
Dad, Dad...

27
00:01:38,373 --> 00:01:40,613
Oh, by the way, about Team Leader Ko.

28
00:01:42,783 --> 00:01:46,613
Do you know anything about how he was adopted by President Ko?

29
00:01:47,153 --> 00:01:50,323
What? Why do you ask?

30
00:01:53,593 --> 00:01:55,023
(Gangsu Construction Apartment Construction Site)

31
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:07,903
It can't be...

32
00:02:08,943 --> 00:02:09,943
Dad.

33
00:02:13,843 --> 00:02:14,843
Mr. Jo.

34
00:02:16,943 --> 00:02:19,753
Team Leader Ko, are you all right? Did you have a nightmare?

35
00:02:19,983 --> 00:02:21,113
Yes, a little...

36
00:02:22,013 --> 00:02:23,023
But...

37
00:02:24,183 --> 00:02:27,523
I came to talk to Eun Ae and heard a strange noise.

38
00:02:28,193 --> 00:02:30,993
I'm sorry for coming in without asking while you were asleep.

39
00:02:31,493 --> 00:02:32,493
It's all right.

40
00:02:34,633 --> 00:02:36,533
I have something to ask you.

41
00:02:37,163 --> 00:02:39,033
After your father passed away,

42
00:02:40,103 --> 00:02:42,443
where did you live, and how were you adopted?

43
00:02:42,973 --> 00:02:44,143
Do you happen to remember?

44
00:02:45,473 --> 00:02:47,743
Yes. After the funeral,

45
00:02:47,743 --> 00:02:49,313
I stayed with my uncle for a little while,

46
00:02:49,543 --> 00:02:50,743
and then I went to an orphanage.

47
00:02:51,383 --> 00:02:53,483
Starlight Orphanage on Ganghwa Island.

48
00:02:53,913 --> 00:02:57,323
A few months later, my grandfather came to get me.

49
00:02:57,853 --> 00:03:00,753
- Get back here. - Let's take it easy.

50
00:03:03,993 --> 00:03:06,593
Let's go. Let's go to my house.

51
00:03:09,763 --> 00:03:10,803
I said, let's go home.

52
00:03:16,773 --> 00:03:18,443
But why do you ask?

53
00:03:19,173 --> 00:03:21,743
I just heard from Eun Ae...

54
00:03:22,513 --> 00:03:25,183
that you seem to have lost your memory after the accident.

55
00:03:26,513 --> 00:03:28,953
Yes, I remember everything else,

56
00:03:29,583 --> 00:03:32,953
but the scene of the accident itself is completely gone.

57
00:03:33,493 --> 00:03:35,223
So you mean the place where it happened,

58
00:03:35,563 --> 00:03:38,763
or what the situation was like, you have no memory of it at all?

59
00:03:39,093 --> 00:03:41,563
Yes, I couldn't remember anything at all,

60
00:03:42,133 --> 00:03:43,463
but recently in my dreams,

61
00:03:44,063 --> 00:03:47,033
I saw my father's last moments.

62
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:49,003
Faintly.

63
00:03:54,013 --> 00:03:57,183
Oh, I'm sorry. It seems I've made things harder for you.

64
00:03:57,883 --> 00:03:59,553
I'll head down now, so get some sleep.

65
00:03:59,853 --> 00:04:02,723
- Oh, yes. Good night, sir. - All right.

66
00:04:02,783 --> 00:04:03,783
Yes.

67
00:04:24,503 --> 00:04:26,873
I could hear police sirens coming from somewhere.

68
00:04:28,413 --> 00:04:31,713
It was vaguely an accident scene,

69
00:04:32,753 --> 00:04:34,083
and I saw people.

70
00:04:35,723 --> 00:04:36,953
But...

71
00:04:37,783 --> 00:04:38,783
who were those people?

72
00:04:40,153 --> 00:04:41,623
I want to see them more clearly,

73
00:04:42,863 --> 00:04:44,223
but I just can't remember.

74
00:04:46,863 --> 00:04:49,833
Do you happen to know, Father?

75
00:05:08,783 --> 00:05:09,783
(Heart Mailbox)

76
00:05:09,853 --> 00:05:11,883
(Send Your Heart Here)

77
00:05:12,223 --> 00:05:13,323
(Night Intersection Accidents: Use Caution)

78
00:05:13,393 --> 00:05:15,153
(Guide To Early Response In A Traffic Accident)

79
00:05:15,223 --> 00:05:16,563
(Traffic Accident Compensation: How Much Can You Get?)

80
00:05:17,593 --> 00:05:19,693
Oh, there are no articles.

81
00:05:19,693 --> 00:05:21,133
You'd think there would be at least one.

82
00:05:22,193 --> 00:05:24,063
Hey, Joy, I need your help.

83
00:05:24,333 --> 00:05:26,133
Can you find any articles about...

84
00:05:26,133 --> 00:05:28,533
a traffic accident that happened on May 16, 2001?

85
00:05:28,733 --> 00:05:30,973
Yes, I will search now.

86
00:05:32,413 --> 00:05:35,913
I'm sorry, Mom. I cannot find anything.

87
00:05:36,383 --> 00:05:40,413
For cases that are too old or are simple traffic accidents,

88
00:05:40,853 --> 00:05:44,823
they have not been digitized, which limits my search.

89
00:05:45,223 --> 00:05:48,493
Please provide more specific information.

90
00:05:48,923 --> 00:05:51,763
If I knew that, I would've found it myself, Joy.

91
00:05:51,923 --> 00:05:55,803
Don't be too disappointed. Please keep trying.

92
00:05:55,933 --> 00:06:00,703
- You can do it, Mom. - Right. Thanks. That's comforting.

93
00:06:02,173 --> 00:06:03,173
What?

94
00:06:06,143 --> 00:06:07,343
(Heart Mailbox)

95
00:06:07,413 --> 00:06:09,883
(Send Your Heart Here)

96
00:06:09,943 --> 00:06:10,943
(User List)

97
00:06:11,313 --> 00:06:12,513
Did he have a bad dream again?

98
00:06:14,383 --> 00:06:17,323
- Safe. - What? What do you mean, safe?

99
00:06:18,423 --> 00:06:21,353
Mom gave me a curfew,

100
00:06:21,423 --> 00:06:23,563
so I have to be home by 11pm, no matter what.

101
00:06:24,563 --> 00:06:25,963
I made it.

102
00:06:26,033 --> 00:06:28,463
Mom gave you a sudden curfew? Why?

103
00:06:28,563 --> 00:06:29,863
I don't know.

104
00:06:30,433 --> 00:06:32,503
Why is Mom so inconsistent?

105
00:06:32,773 --> 00:06:35,843
She's so liberal with you, but a total traditionalist with me.

106
00:06:36,773 --> 00:06:39,473
In the 21st century, of all times,

107
00:06:39,543 --> 00:06:42,213
an 11pm curfew for a writer who has a collaborator?

108
00:06:42,743 --> 00:06:44,983
Does that even make sense?

109
00:06:45,143 --> 00:06:49,013
Well, if Mom gave you a curfew, she must have had a reason.

110
00:06:49,723 --> 00:06:50,723
Hold on.

111
00:06:52,853 --> 00:06:53,853
Yes, Bung Woo.

112
00:06:56,093 --> 00:06:57,923
You want to have a video conference?

113
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:03,263
It's just that I'm not alone right now.

114
00:07:04,003 --> 00:07:06,073
What? Go ahead, don't mind me.

115
00:07:06,333 --> 00:07:07,333
- Are you sure? - Yes.

116
00:07:08,603 --> 00:07:10,803
But you have to finish within an hour.

117
00:07:10,873 --> 00:07:12,473
Of course. Thanks.

118
00:07:13,113 --> 00:07:15,473
Yes, I can. I'll hang up and get on my laptop.

119
00:07:31,363 --> 00:07:33,363
So...

120
00:07:33,593 --> 00:07:35,633
You want to change the story development...

121
00:07:35,633 --> 00:07:36,763
we just discussed?

122
00:07:37,033 --> 00:07:38,033
How so?

123
00:07:38,603 --> 00:07:42,673
When the youngest daughter and son face opposition from their families,

124
00:07:42,803 --> 00:07:45,743
you said it was right for them to have a clean break.

125
00:07:46,543 --> 00:07:48,273
But I don't feel that's right, you know?

126
00:07:48,673 --> 00:07:50,983
If they're truly in love, why would they break up?

127
00:07:51,543 --> 00:07:54,513
That's not cool, that's pathetic.

128
00:07:55,083 --> 00:07:56,083
Pathetic?

129
00:07:57,253 --> 00:07:59,393
The youngest daughter acts cool on the outside,

130
00:07:59,453 --> 00:08:02,493
but it's a decision she made after a huge internal struggle.

131
00:08:03,093 --> 00:08:05,293
She's afraid of hurting him because of her situation.

132
00:08:05,623 --> 00:08:08,493
That's why she hides her feelings and chooses to break up.

133
00:08:08,793 --> 00:08:10,533
Exactly, see?

134
00:08:10,533 --> 00:08:13,533
Why would she cowardly hide behind that sadness?

135
00:08:14,273 --> 00:08:16,373
I think it would be better if the two of them...

136
00:08:16,373 --> 00:08:17,773
just gave everything up...

137
00:08:18,243 --> 00:08:20,143
and ran away. Yes.

138
00:08:20,243 --> 00:08:24,013
What? You mean they should elope or something?

139
00:08:24,143 --> 00:08:25,743
Yes. And why?

140
00:08:25,953 --> 00:08:27,413
Because I like you

141
00:08:27,783 --> 00:08:29,013
I like you

142
00:08:29,013 --> 00:08:31,353
I like you because you're pretty

143
00:08:32,753 --> 00:08:34,053
But still...

144
00:08:34,053 --> 00:08:36,523
You can't just do that because you like someone that much...

145
00:08:38,163 --> 00:08:39,463
Oh, for crying out loud.

146
00:08:40,693 --> 00:08:42,803
Isn't that a bit too extreme?

147
00:08:42,803 --> 00:08:44,263
But I'm crazy about you.

148
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:48,503
What am I supposed to do, then?

149
00:08:49,643 --> 00:08:50,643
I like you...

150
00:08:51,843 --> 00:08:53,313
because you're you.

151
00:08:54,573 --> 00:08:56,313
Let's see. What is all this?

152
00:08:59,753 --> 00:09:02,353
Goodness, Manager Seo...

153
00:09:03,383 --> 00:09:04,423
Jo Eun Ae?

154
00:09:09,623 --> 00:09:12,093
It's such a small world.

155
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:13,933
How could you and Manager Seo's younger brother...

156
00:09:14,993 --> 00:09:18,103
No wonder. At Grandfather's living funeral,

157
00:09:18,163 --> 00:09:20,173
I noticed you two were always together.

158
00:09:20,773 --> 00:09:22,743
What are you talking about? We weren't.

159
00:09:23,043 --> 00:09:26,243
We just had story meetings whenever we had a free moment.

160
00:09:26,713 --> 00:09:31,043
I see. And your video conference is about your webtoon?

161
00:09:31,143 --> 00:09:34,083
- And that passionate confession? - What passionate confession?

162
00:09:34,553 --> 00:09:36,883
That's all going to be part of our story.

163
00:09:36,953 --> 00:09:39,553
Is that so?

164
00:09:41,453 --> 00:09:42,493
Stop it.

165
00:09:45,023 --> 00:09:46,593
Anyway, why are you in my room?

166
00:09:46,933 --> 00:09:50,733
I came to have a beer with you, but I had to see and hear that.

167
00:09:57,903 --> 00:10:01,313
But why do you like that writer who gave you such a hard time?

168
00:10:02,073 --> 00:10:06,053
It was a real tearjerker. So incredibly passionate.

169
00:10:06,313 --> 00:10:07,613
What are you talking about?

170
00:10:07,913 --> 00:10:10,753
The brilliant Seo Seung Ri...

171
00:10:10,753 --> 00:10:13,223
can't tell the difference between the real world and a webtoon?

172
00:10:13,893 --> 00:10:16,823
That was purely a scene from my work...

173
00:10:16,893 --> 00:10:19,663
Hey, don't you know I can read you like a book?

174
00:10:19,733 --> 00:10:20,793
Don't even try it.

175
00:10:21,593 --> 00:10:24,433
Fine, fine, you're right. So what? I like Bung Nim.

176
00:10:24,503 --> 00:10:25,703
What? What are you going to do about it?

177
00:10:26,373 --> 00:10:27,403
Bung Nim?

178
00:10:27,403 --> 00:10:30,543
Yes. Eun Nim, Bung Nim, Seung Woo, Bung Woo.

179
00:10:31,473 --> 00:10:36,383
We're raising a pet goldfish together in our studio.

180
00:10:36,513 --> 00:10:37,713
A pet goldfish?

181
00:10:38,983 --> 00:10:42,453
You're unbelievable. Are you two actually dating?

182
00:10:43,153 --> 00:10:46,653
No, not yet. Well, I confessed my feelings,

183
00:10:46,653 --> 00:10:49,423
but Bung Nim hasn't given me a definite answer yet.

184
00:10:49,893 --> 00:10:51,963
What? What did you just say?

185
00:10:52,563 --> 00:10:54,793
A confession? Who said you could?

186
00:10:56,033 --> 00:10:57,363
Why?

187
00:10:57,363 --> 00:10:59,033
Why is me liking someone...

188
00:10:59,333 --> 00:11:00,703
a reason for you two to gang up on me like this?

189
00:11:00,933 --> 00:11:03,173
I don't like her. I just don't.

190
00:11:03,173 --> 00:11:05,243
Why? What's wrong with Bung Nim? What's so bad about her?

191
00:11:05,303 --> 00:11:07,073
I don't like the way she looks.

192
00:11:07,213 --> 00:11:09,173
What's wrong with how she looks?

193
00:11:09,513 --> 00:11:11,483
It's hard to find someone that beautiful.

194
00:11:12,043 --> 00:11:14,583
Her eyes are so big and bright.

195
00:11:14,683 --> 00:11:17,253
What? You don't like her because her eyes are bright?

196
00:11:17,383 --> 00:11:19,793
So what, you'd rather her eyes were dull and lifeless?

197
00:11:19,853 --> 00:11:22,623
- Is that what you'd prefer? - Her hair was a mess,

198
00:11:22,963 --> 00:11:24,063
and she was clumsy enough...

199
00:11:24,063 --> 00:11:26,193
to get drenched in water, wasn't she?

200
00:11:26,263 --> 00:11:28,993
I can't forget her voice when she bossed you around,

201
00:11:29,363 --> 00:11:30,803
thinking she was all high and mighty.

202
00:11:30,863 --> 00:11:33,803
Right? From what I remember, he was completely...

203
00:11:33,873 --> 00:11:36,203
at that writer's mercy until just a while ago.

204
00:11:36,573 --> 00:11:37,743
What was it you said?

205
00:11:38,073 --> 00:11:40,843
Something about her being someone you want to crush but can't?

206
00:11:41,343 --> 00:11:42,343
You remember saying that, right?

207
00:11:42,643 --> 00:11:46,213
You all have such inconveniently good memories.

208
00:11:48,013 --> 00:11:49,213
That's not true.

209
00:11:49,283 --> 00:11:52,523
It's really, really not like that anymore.

210
00:11:52,583 --> 00:11:53,593
Quiet!

211
00:11:53,893 --> 00:11:54,893
She is absolutely out of the question.

212
00:11:55,353 --> 00:11:58,663
Why? Why is she out of the question?

213
00:12:01,033 --> 00:12:03,703
Dad, why are you standing here?

214
00:12:04,263 --> 00:12:05,363
Well...

215
00:12:06,033 --> 00:12:09,173
It was nice hearing the three of you being so lively for a change.

216
00:12:09,973 --> 00:12:10,973
Oh, Dad.

217
00:12:11,343 --> 00:12:14,173
- Go on to bed. It's late. - Okay. Good night, Dad.

218
00:12:31,493 --> 00:12:33,093
I was wondering where you went so early.

219
00:12:33,433 --> 00:12:34,433
When did you get up?

220
00:12:34,763 --> 00:12:35,763
A while ago.

221
00:12:37,663 --> 00:12:38,663
What's with that necklace?

222
00:12:40,173 --> 00:12:41,233
I...

223
00:12:42,003 --> 00:12:45,403
took the necklace and the compact, threw them at my mother,

224
00:12:46,273 --> 00:12:48,313
and told her I never wanted to see her again.

225
00:12:48,943 --> 00:12:51,483
But later, I asked for them back.

226
00:12:53,213 --> 00:12:54,653
For the past 50 years,

227
00:12:55,113 --> 00:12:59,993
this necklace was the only thing that connected me to my mother.

228
00:13:02,093 --> 00:13:05,423
The thought of being legally family with my mother,

229
00:13:05,593 --> 00:13:08,593
being bound together on one document,

230
00:13:09,463 --> 00:13:12,163
somehow made me feel quite secure.

231
00:13:13,903 --> 00:13:15,073
I thought I would never...

232
00:13:15,573 --> 00:13:17,543
have to worry about losing her again.

233
00:13:19,613 --> 00:13:21,843
But now, I've made up my mind.

234
00:13:23,883 --> 00:13:28,013
Okay. Whatever you decide, just follow your heart.

235
00:13:33,723 --> 00:13:35,293
You're giving up becoming...

236
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:38,463
a part of our family register as our daughter?

237
00:13:40,433 --> 00:13:41,833
I'm not giving up.

238
00:13:42,463 --> 00:13:45,633
I'll just keep living as I am now.

239
00:13:45,633 --> 00:13:46,673
Yeon Soon.

240
00:13:47,433 --> 00:13:50,443
Is this because of Gyeol and Eun Ae?

241
00:13:52,243 --> 00:13:53,243
Yes.

242
00:13:53,643 --> 00:13:56,113
At first, I was also completely against...

243
00:13:57,213 --> 00:14:00,013
them dating.

244
00:14:00,553 --> 00:14:01,913
But when I heard Team Leader Ko...

245
00:14:02,513 --> 00:14:06,753
confess to my husband that he was adopted,

246
00:14:07,253 --> 00:14:09,253
you have no idea how much my heart ached.

247
00:14:10,623 --> 00:14:14,133
Perhaps because I've also been adopted...

248
00:14:14,133 --> 00:14:15,833
and then had it reversed,

249
00:14:16,463 --> 00:14:19,703
I felt I had to protect him from getting hurt anymore.

250
00:14:20,333 --> 00:14:24,503
Besides, I'm my mother's daughter, but not the Chairman's by blood,

251
00:14:25,043 --> 00:14:26,843
so there's no issue with those two anyway.

252
00:14:27,013 --> 00:14:29,913
In that case, the kids' issue doesn't matter.

253
00:14:30,513 --> 00:14:33,513
Yeon Soon, you can still be registered as my daughter.

254
00:14:34,183 --> 00:14:37,923
That's easier said than done. Like President Ko said yesterday,

255
00:14:37,983 --> 00:14:41,353
we can't completely ignore public perception.

256
00:14:42,123 --> 00:14:44,823
Now that I've found you, Mom,

257
00:14:45,223 --> 00:14:47,563
it's no big deal to me whether my name is...

258
00:14:47,563 --> 00:14:48,963
on some document or not.

259
00:14:50,533 --> 00:14:55,003
I won't be the one to scar those kids' hearts.

260
00:14:55,733 --> 00:14:56,943
You understand, don't you?

261
00:14:58,073 --> 00:15:00,013
I do understand, but...

262
00:15:00,973 --> 00:15:02,173
Still...

263
00:15:05,043 --> 00:15:07,383
Mother, Father. I'm home.

264
00:15:08,413 --> 00:15:10,653
Oh my. Ms. Kang Yeon Ja.

265
00:15:10,983 --> 00:15:13,853
Well now, what brings you here?

266
00:15:13,953 --> 00:15:17,023
Does a child need a reason to visit their parents' home?

267
00:15:17,763 --> 00:15:20,833
She has every right to come.

268
00:15:20,833 --> 00:15:21,863
What?

269
00:15:22,393 --> 00:15:23,563
Yes, Father.

270
00:15:24,203 --> 00:15:25,733
Of course. You're right.

271
00:15:26,033 --> 00:15:28,273
This is her mother's home, after all.

272
00:15:30,373 --> 00:15:33,613
I understand what you mean.

273
00:15:34,443 --> 00:15:35,843
I'll be heading in,

274
00:15:36,443 --> 00:15:38,043
so you can talk more with your mother.

275
00:15:40,783 --> 00:15:42,453
I'll get going as well.

276
00:15:42,753 --> 00:15:45,853
I'll leave you two to have your mother-daughter time.

277
00:15:48,893 --> 00:15:50,993
Why don't you think about it a little more?

278
00:15:52,363 --> 00:15:53,363
No.

279
00:15:53,963 --> 00:15:56,563
We should just stay as we are.

280
00:15:57,403 --> 00:15:59,363
We can see each other like this anytime,

281
00:15:59,363 --> 00:16:01,433
without any paperwork.

282
00:16:03,843 --> 00:16:04,843
Paperwork?

283
00:16:05,373 --> 00:16:07,073
Did you just say...

284
00:16:07,413 --> 00:16:11,313
you don't want to be added to our family register?

285
00:16:11,413 --> 00:16:12,913
Is that what I heard?

286
00:16:13,183 --> 00:16:16,013
- Giving up the register? - Yes, that's exactly right,

287
00:16:16,323 --> 00:16:19,993
so don't tell the kids we're some dysfunctional family.

288
00:16:20,553 --> 00:16:23,323
Oh my. Goodness, of course.

289
00:16:23,393 --> 00:16:25,063
I'm all for it.

290
00:16:25,063 --> 00:16:28,563
From now on, I'm rooting for your daughter and our Gyeol.

291
00:16:28,563 --> 00:16:31,063
Yes, thank you so much for your support.

292
00:16:31,433 --> 00:16:34,773
- Mom, I'm going to go now. - Why?

293
00:16:35,203 --> 00:16:37,973
You're already here. Stay and have a meal with us.

294
00:16:38,173 --> 00:16:40,373
I have a lot to do. I'll come again.

295
00:16:41,573 --> 00:16:43,313
Okay, get home safely.

296
00:16:44,383 --> 00:16:46,583
Goodbye, miss. Goodbye.

297
00:16:52,283 --> 00:16:56,423
Honey. Kang Yeon Ja finally dropped her claim.

298
00:16:57,823 --> 00:16:59,223
That's right.

299
00:16:59,223 --> 00:17:02,233
She's giving up her spot on the family register.

300
00:17:02,433 --> 00:17:03,433
On her own.

301
00:17:04,703 --> 00:17:05,863
Is that really true?

302
00:17:06,573 --> 00:17:08,573
How could she give up so easily?

303
00:17:08,803 --> 00:17:11,573
It looks like it's because of her daughter and Gyeol.

304
00:17:11,643 --> 00:17:13,003
So they can date for real.

305
00:17:13,673 --> 00:17:16,073
Really? Then I guess what we said yesterday...

306
00:17:16,143 --> 00:17:17,683
really hit the mark.

307
00:17:17,683 --> 00:17:19,283
I know.

308
00:17:19,283 --> 00:17:20,713
Especially when I said our family was a complete mess.

309
00:17:20,783 --> 00:17:22,553
I think that's what got to her the most.

310
00:17:23,253 --> 00:17:24,283
Crystal.

311
00:17:24,553 --> 00:17:28,223
Even so, don't be so obvious about how happy you are.

312
00:17:29,423 --> 00:17:30,523
It's too transparent.

313
00:17:30,763 --> 00:17:34,233
So what? I'm an open book.

314
00:17:34,293 --> 00:17:36,293
There's nothing for me to hide.

315
00:17:36,293 --> 00:17:37,633
But the important thing is that...

316
00:17:37,633 --> 00:17:40,703
our biggest headache has been resolved.

317
00:17:40,873 --> 00:17:42,203
So, honey, I'm hanging up.

318
00:17:44,203 --> 00:17:46,943
Oh, my goodness.

319
00:17:46,943 --> 00:17:48,413
How foolish.

320
00:17:48,573 --> 00:17:50,083
If she were registered as the Chairman's daughter,

321
00:17:50,083 --> 00:17:51,083
the inheritance would be huge.

322
00:17:51,143 --> 00:17:52,383
And she's throwing that away herself?

323
00:17:57,823 --> 00:17:59,023
Oh, this.

324
00:17:59,023 --> 00:18:00,053
(Our Happy Days Real Estate, Grandma Pancake)

325
00:18:00,853 --> 00:18:04,323
Eun Hyung, did you bring this flower for me?

326
00:18:08,193 --> 00:18:09,493
What's with her?

327
00:18:10,403 --> 00:18:11,533
No matter how I look at it,

328
00:18:12,163 --> 00:18:14,073
she seems to have heatstroke.

329
00:18:20,713 --> 00:18:21,713
Hey.

330
00:18:22,573 --> 00:18:23,713
Yes? What is it, Grandma?

331
00:18:24,413 --> 00:18:26,383
But since yesterday,

332
00:18:26,653 --> 00:18:29,353
why have you been staring at that flower?

333
00:18:30,523 --> 00:18:34,693
You didn't actually pay for a flower you can't even eat, did you?

334
00:18:34,993 --> 00:18:37,063
Eun Hyung...

335
00:18:37,423 --> 00:18:40,193
brought this for me from the funeral home yesterday.

336
00:18:42,993 --> 00:18:44,003
You.

337
00:18:44,963 --> 00:18:46,163
Listen to me carefully.

338
00:18:47,603 --> 00:18:48,773
Eun Hyung.

339
00:18:49,473 --> 00:18:54,373
I know very well that he's kind, diligent, and smart.

340
00:18:54,643 --> 00:18:55,913
Yes, so?

341
00:18:56,013 --> 00:19:00,483
But even if the world turns upside down...

342
00:19:00,553 --> 00:19:04,123
and every other couple gets divorced,

343
00:19:04,183 --> 00:19:05,883
I will never approve.

344
00:19:06,383 --> 00:19:10,463
Approve of what? Please make some sense.

345
00:19:10,523 --> 00:19:14,233
A divorced man with a child is absolutely not...

346
00:19:17,833 --> 00:19:19,733
What were you talking about?

347
00:19:21,033 --> 00:19:23,573
We weren't talking about anything.

348
00:19:23,873 --> 00:19:26,673
How is your father doing?

349
00:19:27,013 --> 00:19:28,013
Pardon?

350
00:19:28,743 --> 00:19:31,543
The Chairman? Yes, he's doing much better.

351
00:19:32,783 --> 00:19:34,713
Just call him your father.

352
00:19:35,113 --> 00:19:38,783
He's been with your mother for over 50 years.

353
00:19:38,853 --> 00:19:40,893
Of course he's your father.

354
00:19:41,753 --> 00:19:45,593
And soon you'll be officially on the family register.

355
00:19:45,963 --> 00:19:47,193
Why would I do that?

356
00:19:48,463 --> 00:19:50,803
- I refused. - You refused?

357
00:19:51,403 --> 00:19:52,963
What? Why?

358
00:19:53,773 --> 00:19:54,773
Just because.

359
00:19:55,203 --> 00:19:58,073
At my age, what's the point of putting my name on some document?

360
00:19:58,843 --> 00:20:01,113
Oh, dear. But that's not right.

361
00:20:01,443 --> 00:20:03,913
You have to be registered as the Chairman's daughter,

362
00:20:03,913 --> 00:20:05,243
so that later...

363
00:20:05,313 --> 00:20:07,983
Then what about our Eun Ae and Team Leader Ko?

364
00:20:08,953 --> 00:20:11,753
Ma'am. To help Eun Ae's love story succeed,

365
00:20:11,983 --> 00:20:14,153
you gave up your position as a conglomerate heiress?

366
00:20:14,223 --> 00:20:15,223
That's incredible.

367
00:20:15,293 --> 00:20:16,963
Heiress? What are you talking about?

368
00:20:17,023 --> 00:20:18,763
Gosh, just bring me the bean sprouts.

369
00:20:18,963 --> 00:20:20,593
We can prep them together when we have time.

370
00:20:22,293 --> 00:20:24,633
(Gangsu Construction)

371
00:20:27,073 --> 00:20:29,973
Okay, this is excellent. Documents should be...

372
00:20:30,603 --> 00:20:33,473
simple, clear, and neat.

373
00:20:34,713 --> 00:20:35,773
Perfect.

374
00:20:38,013 --> 00:20:41,453
And another thing. I have to say, Secretary Jo,

375
00:20:41,453 --> 00:20:43,013
your wife is quite something.

376
00:20:43,623 --> 00:20:45,823
How could she give up her place as the Gangsu Group...

377
00:20:45,883 --> 00:20:48,153
Chairman's daughter for her own daughter's love life?

378
00:20:48,453 --> 00:20:49,453
Pardon?

379
00:20:50,193 --> 00:20:51,593
Does not being on the family register...

380
00:20:51,593 --> 00:20:52,993
erase a mother-daughter bond?

381
00:20:53,063 --> 00:20:55,833
My wife has not abandoned her mother.

382
00:20:56,563 --> 00:20:58,833
Right. Well, she only gave it up on paper.

383
00:20:58,833 --> 00:20:59,903
I suppose a daughter is still a daughter.

384
00:20:59,973 --> 00:21:00,973
Exactly.

385
00:21:01,403 --> 00:21:06,103
But you know, whether her name is on that family register or not...

386
00:21:06,173 --> 00:21:09,343
makes a huge difference in the outcome, to put it bluntly.

387
00:21:09,713 --> 00:21:12,643
Things like inheritance or shares in Gangsu Group.

388
00:21:13,183 --> 00:21:15,583
Honestly. Anyway, that audacity...

389
00:21:16,213 --> 00:21:17,723
is very impressive.

390
00:21:20,293 --> 00:21:23,663
Excuse me, I have a question.

391
00:21:24,863 --> 00:21:25,863
A question?

392
00:21:26,763 --> 00:21:30,163
May I ask why the approval documents from the Finance Team...

393
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:31,603
haven't been coming through lately?

394
00:21:33,503 --> 00:21:35,733
The Finance Team documents?

395
00:21:36,333 --> 00:21:38,903
I've switched the Finance Team's approval documents...

396
00:21:38,903 --> 00:21:40,473
to an electronic system.

397
00:21:41,213 --> 00:21:44,413
These documents come in several times a day,

398
00:21:44,483 --> 00:21:48,013
and I thought it was inefficient for me to sign them on paper.

399
00:21:48,413 --> 00:21:49,953
Making an exception to the approval process...

400
00:21:50,023 --> 00:21:51,023
for just one department...

401
00:21:51,523 --> 00:21:52,883
could be problematic.

402
00:21:54,193 --> 00:21:56,253
Secretary Jo. No, my dear brother-in-law.

403
00:21:56,923 --> 00:22:00,263
I'm your boss and your older brother-in-law.

404
00:22:00,593 --> 00:22:02,633
Before you start telling me what to do,

405
00:22:03,193 --> 00:22:05,203
perhaps you should remember your place first.

406
00:22:05,533 --> 00:22:08,033
Then allow me to say something as your younger brother-in-law.

407
00:22:09,103 --> 00:22:11,203
The Chairman may not be coming to the office right now,

408
00:22:11,543 --> 00:22:12,673
but the company...

409
00:22:13,543 --> 00:22:15,643
is still running smoothly under his system.

410
00:22:15,713 --> 00:22:16,813
For you, the president,

411
00:22:17,613 --> 00:22:18,883
to use such an exceptional method...

412
00:22:18,943 --> 00:22:21,313
unilaterally and without approval is...

413
00:22:21,383 --> 00:22:23,623
Hold on.

414
00:22:25,183 --> 00:22:26,353
Mr. Charles?

415
00:22:27,723 --> 00:22:29,323
My friend.

416
00:22:30,393 --> 00:22:31,563
Okay.

417
00:22:32,963 --> 00:22:34,133
Global business?

418
00:22:35,663 --> 00:22:39,563
Very important. Good job.

419
00:22:41,073 --> 00:22:44,073
Can't you see I'm on the phone? Get out. Hurry, get out.

420
00:22:44,743 --> 00:22:47,213
Excuse me? No.

421
00:22:47,713 --> 00:22:48,713
Really?

422
00:22:49,473 --> 00:22:50,513
For real?

423
00:22:53,383 --> 00:22:54,913
My gosh.

424
00:22:57,183 --> 00:22:58,283
Oh, Charlie.

425
00:22:58,653 --> 00:23:01,593
Was it Charles? Charles. Gosh, seriously. Darn it.

426
00:23:02,393 --> 00:23:04,123
What am I going to do?

427
00:23:04,193 --> 00:23:07,163
How do I get off his radar? Goodness.

428
00:23:09,963 --> 00:23:12,903
What? Taking a half-day off again? Why? Is something going on?

429
00:23:13,263 --> 00:23:14,473
It's a personal matter.

430
00:23:14,633 --> 00:23:17,903
I know, but what kind of personal matter...

431
00:23:17,973 --> 00:23:20,313
has you taking time off when we should be preparing...

432
00:23:20,313 --> 00:23:22,273
for the third competition?

433
00:23:23,143 --> 00:23:25,383
Do you really need an answer?

434
00:23:26,243 --> 00:23:29,683
Then again, it's obvious you won't answer,

435
00:23:29,683 --> 00:23:31,083
but here I am asking anyway.

436
00:23:31,583 --> 00:23:33,493
Fine. Don't tell me if you don't want to.

437
00:23:35,293 --> 00:23:37,763
I'm looking for records related to my father's accident.

438
00:23:38,793 --> 00:23:41,593
What? Records about your father's accident?

439
00:23:41,993 --> 00:23:43,533
You don't mean your biological father?

440
00:23:44,533 --> 00:23:45,533
Yes.

441
00:23:46,663 --> 00:23:50,143
So you're telling me the reason you've been taking time off...

442
00:23:50,603 --> 00:23:53,743
is to dig into an incident from 25 years ago?

443
00:23:54,643 --> 00:23:56,213
I'm not digging.

444
00:23:56,273 --> 00:23:59,613
I'm trying to find a missing piece of the puzzle of my lost past.

445
00:24:00,653 --> 00:24:03,053
A puzzle of your lost past...

446
00:24:05,153 --> 00:24:07,653
Does that mean you lost all your memories of the accident?

447
00:24:10,363 --> 00:24:11,863
So I guess that's true.

448
00:24:12,663 --> 00:24:13,833
But why are you...

449
00:24:14,133 --> 00:24:16,493
suddenly looking into an accident you don't even remember?

450
00:24:17,163 --> 00:24:18,363
May I go now?

451
00:24:18,833 --> 00:24:21,003
Oh, of course. Yes. Go on.

452
00:24:21,503 --> 00:24:22,903
- Thanks. - Sure.

453
00:24:25,343 --> 00:24:27,213
Why did you come out here? You were in the middle of work.

454
00:24:27,313 --> 00:24:29,043
I just felt bad sending you off alone,

455
00:24:29,043 --> 00:24:30,613
so I came to see you out.

456
00:24:31,113 --> 00:24:32,743
What am I, a kid?

457
00:24:32,743 --> 00:24:34,353
You don't have to worry about me going alone.

458
00:24:34,353 --> 00:24:36,983
I wanted to go with you, but it's right before the competition.

459
00:24:37,053 --> 00:24:38,923
I didn't think it would be right for me to be away from my desk too.

460
00:24:39,083 --> 00:24:42,053
It's fine. It's not like I'll get the results immediately.

461
00:24:42,323 --> 00:24:44,093
I'm just filing a freedom of information request.

462
00:24:44,463 --> 00:24:45,693
You don't have to come with me.

463
00:24:46,293 --> 00:24:49,363
Did you forget we promised to always be together?

464
00:24:49,463 --> 00:24:52,463
This isn't a good place for this.

465
00:24:52,533 --> 00:24:54,903
All right. I'll let it slide, just for today.

466
00:24:55,633 --> 00:24:58,303
You can't just take my hand and then let go.

467
00:24:58,303 --> 00:24:59,703
Once you grab on, it's for keeps.

468
00:24:59,843 --> 00:25:03,543
Even when you're alone, don't forget I'm always with you.

469
00:25:04,183 --> 00:25:06,313
- Next to Roary... - Is Hoppy.

470
00:25:06,883 --> 00:25:08,113
Don't worry.

471
00:25:08,113 --> 00:25:10,553
It's like I have "Jo Eun Ae" tattooed on me.

472
00:25:10,753 --> 00:25:13,083
If you get there and they say there are no files...

473
00:25:13,153 --> 00:25:16,553
or that they can't be disclosed, don't get upset.

474
00:25:16,993 --> 00:25:18,863
We'll find a way somehow.

475
00:25:19,593 --> 00:25:20,733
All right.

476
00:25:21,033 --> 00:25:23,233
Don't worry so much and go back to work.

477
00:25:23,493 --> 00:25:26,063
If you slack off, you'll be in trouble.

478
00:25:28,033 --> 00:25:29,273
Be safe, Team Leader Ko.

479
00:25:36,343 --> 00:25:39,713
- Has everyone gone to lunch? - Yes.

480
00:25:40,883 --> 00:25:42,353
Here's the comparative analysis of the candidate sites...

481
00:25:42,353 --> 00:25:43,453
for our retirement community.

482
00:25:43,453 --> 00:25:45,753
- Please take a look. - Thank you.

483
00:25:46,923 --> 00:25:49,353
By the way, you mentioned yesterday...

484
00:25:49,853 --> 00:25:53,633
that Team Leader Ko seemed to be on a call with the police.

485
00:25:54,163 --> 00:25:57,103
- Yes. - It turns out you heard correctly.

486
00:25:57,333 --> 00:26:00,203
He's looking into his father's accident.

487
00:26:00,203 --> 00:26:01,203
His biological father.

488
00:26:01,733 --> 00:26:04,503
- Biological father's accident? - Yes.

489
00:26:05,143 --> 00:26:07,543
Gyeol was also at the scene of the accident,

490
00:26:07,543 --> 00:26:09,673
but it seems he's repressed the memory all this time.

491
00:26:09,973 --> 00:26:14,553
It looks like he's trying to recover that lost memory.

492
00:26:14,853 --> 00:26:17,753
- He lost his memory? - Yes.

493
00:26:18,723 --> 00:26:21,393
Gyeol and I have been brothers for 25 years,

494
00:26:21,723 --> 00:26:23,153
and I'm only just finding this out today.

495
00:26:24,523 --> 00:26:27,993
Still, it's a relief he has Jo Eun Ae with him.

496
00:26:29,133 --> 00:26:32,163
- Yes, I think so too. - Anyway...

497
00:26:33,333 --> 00:26:36,603
I think we need to visit the candidate sites in person...

498
00:26:36,603 --> 00:26:39,103
to see if they're suitable.

499
00:26:39,703 --> 00:26:42,773
Would you be able to go survey them with me sometime this week?

500
00:26:43,043 --> 00:26:44,343
Yes, of course.

501
00:26:46,883 --> 00:26:49,083
The approval process only changed for the finance team?

502
00:26:50,083 --> 00:26:52,053
They switched to an electronic approval system.

503
00:26:52,653 --> 00:26:54,523
Apparently, signing the many documents...

504
00:26:54,593 --> 00:26:57,963
that come in daily was deemed inefficient.

505
00:26:58,993 --> 00:27:01,963
The other day, you were asking Secretary Ju...

506
00:27:02,163 --> 00:27:03,703
about the finance director.

507
00:27:04,233 --> 00:27:06,203
Did you find anything unusual then?

508
00:27:06,703 --> 00:27:09,333
I saw some strange irregularities in the minor cash flow,

509
00:27:09,333 --> 00:27:10,543
which I found odd.

510
00:27:11,573 --> 00:27:12,643
Why the sudden interest?

511
00:27:13,273 --> 00:27:15,613
I think the Chairman is on to something...

512
00:27:15,613 --> 00:27:16,873
regarding President Ko.

513
00:27:17,143 --> 00:27:18,743
He asked me to investigate.

514
00:27:20,413 --> 00:27:24,283
Don't tell me President Ko is siphoning off a slush fund.

515
00:27:24,983 --> 00:27:28,253
There's no hard evidence yet, so I have to find it.

516
00:27:30,863 --> 00:27:32,193
Ko Dae Chi, honestly.

517
00:27:35,233 --> 00:27:36,293
Oh, and Gwon Sik.

518
00:27:37,833 --> 00:27:39,803
I have something to ask you.

519
00:27:40,103 --> 00:27:41,533
Yes? What is it?

520
00:27:44,403 --> 00:27:45,673
It's about that child.

521
00:27:50,113 --> 00:27:53,113
Do you happen to know what happened to them?

522
00:27:55,683 --> 00:27:56,983
What child?

523
00:27:59,283 --> 00:28:00,953
The child from 25 years ago.

524
00:28:22,543 --> 00:28:25,583
(Our Happy Days)
